# Class: obo:HMDM_0000090 (thymidine pyrimidine-nucleoside phosphorylase family)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:27004974") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:9817849") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000090 "Thymidine phosphorylase (TP) enzyme catalyzes the phosphorolysis of the nucleosides thymidine (dThd) and deoxyuridine (dUrd) to the corresponding bases thymine and uracil, and deoxyribose-1-phosphate. Thymidine phosphorylase (TP), is also related to Pyrimidine nucleoside phosphorylase (PYNP), which catalyzes the reversible phosphorolysis of pyrimidines in the nucleotide synthesis salvage pathway. In lower organisms (e.g. Bacillus stearothermophilus) PYNP accepts both thymidine and uridine, whereas in mammalian and other higher organisms it is specific for thymidine (designated thymidine phosphorylase, TP). PYNP shares 40% sequence similarity (and presumably significant structural similarity) with human TP.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000090 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000090 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000090 "HMDM:0000090")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000090 "thymidine pyrimidine-nucleoside phosphorylase family")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000090 obo:HMDM_0000012)

